{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00526",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 14.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.98,
      "text": "I'm grand, doctor, really. It was only Bridget here who insisted I come in for the check on the leg after the tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.89,
      "end_seconds": 29.68,
      "duration_seconds": 12.79,
      "text": "Good on Bridget, then. This is the second time it's flared up on that shin, so I'd sooner look than guess. Bridget, you're with him at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 31.93,
      "end_seconds": 46.71,
      "duration_seconds": 14.78,
      "text": "I am, I'm his live-in carer, five days a week. He'd never tell you if it was bad, so I tell you for him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.49,
      "end_seconds": 50.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "There's nothing to tell."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.23,
      "end_seconds": 59.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "Fair enough, we'll see. Is it all right if the healthcare assistant takes down the dressing first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 61.7,
      "end_seconds": 72.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.62,
      "text": "Hello Mr Doyle. I'll unwrap the leg and have the dressing pack ready for the doctor, it won't take a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.69,
      "end_seconds": 78.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Ah, don't be making a fuss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.14,
      "end_seconds": 89.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "While she does that, a couple of questions. Any fever or shivers since I last saw you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.16,
      "end_seconds": 91.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.73,
      "end_seconds": 100.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "And any pain in the leg, or is it just a bit tender?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.99,
      "end_seconds": 106.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "No pain. Nothing worth mentioning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 107.96,
      "end_seconds": 119.31,
      "duration_seconds": 11.35,
      "text": "He doesn't complain, that's the problem. But I'll say he's been walking the garden path every day without limping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.2,
      "end_seconds": 131.49,
      "duration_seconds": 10.29,
      "text": "That's useful to hear from you, thank you. Now, the tablets. Which antibiotic are you finishing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.96,
      "end_seconds": 139.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "The doxycycline, 100 mg, twice a day. I've two days left."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.92,
      "end_seconds": 148.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "Good. And you're taking that because of the penicillin trouble, aren't you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.87,
      "end_seconds": 158.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "I am. Penicillin gave me hives years ago. They told me never again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.14,
      "end_seconds": 173.29,
      "duration_seconds": 13.15,
      "text": "Right, penicillin allergy with hives, I'll make sure that's on the front of your notes. Any other tablets I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 175.65,
      "end_seconds": 187.82,
      "duration_seconds": 12.17,
      "text": "There's the water tablet for the swelling, the furosemide. It's in the morning. I think it's maybe 20 mg? I'd have to check the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.42,
      "end_seconds": 199.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Maybe 20 mg, we'll confirm it against the pharmacy list. Mr Doyle, do you remember?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.47,
      "end_seconds": 205.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I take what Bridget puts in my hand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.11,
      "end_seconds": 212.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Fair. Anything long-term behind the swollen legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.34,
      "end_seconds": 221.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "The heart failure. It's well managed. And I had the hip replaced about ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.29,
      "end_seconds": 230.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Heart failure and the hip replacement, thank you. Let's have a look at the leg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.04,
      "end_seconds": 268.91,
      "duration_seconds": 18.87,
      "text": "Temperature is 36.8 degrees, and your pulse is 76. Now I'm looking at the shin. The redness has faded to a pale pink, and there's no warmth over the skin where it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.33,
      "end_seconds": 274.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Is that good or bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.54,
      "end_seconds": 284.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "Good. It looks like the cellulitis has cleared, which is what we wanted from this course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.11,
      "end_seconds": 290.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I told you it was nothing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.33,
      "end_seconds": 307.15,
      "duration_seconds": 13.82,
      "text": "You did, and I'm still glad we checked. Now let me give you the choices for keeping it from coming back a third time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 309.4,
      "end_seconds": 315.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Please do. I'm tired of the carpet being covered in cotton wool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.3,
      "end_seconds": 336.93,
      "duration_seconds": 19.63,
      "text": "First option, compression stockings in the daytime, which helps the swelling that sets the skin up for infection. Second, moisturise the skin twice a day so it doesn't crack. Third, keep your feet up when you're sitting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.38,
      "end_seconds": 342.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "The stockings are a divil to get on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.71,
      "end_seconds": 353.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "They are. Bridget or the community nurse can help with that. Which of the three would you actually do?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.32,
      "end_seconds": 359.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "The moisturiser. I'd do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 362.27,
      "end_seconds": 371.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "And I'll do the feet up, if I have to tie him to the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.5,
      "end_seconds": 385.71,
      "duration_seconds": 12.21,
      "text": "Then moisturiser every day, feet up when sitting, and finish the doxycycline. We can talk about the stockings another day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.37,
      "end_seconds": 390.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Grand. Will that be everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.84,
      "end_seconds": 397.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "That's everything for today. You look well, Mr Doyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 399.06,
      "end_seconds": 407.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "I'll put a light dressing back on, and a clean sock over it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.56,
      "end_seconds": 411.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Thanks, love."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 413.3,
      "end_seconds": 420.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "I'll bring him in for a cup of tea first, we passed a lovely bakery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.86,
      "end_seconds": 426.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Enjoy it. Take care, both of you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.42,
      "end_seconds": 430.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Good day, doctor."
    }
  ]
}
